{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDUXrQxcrYftXfMmGDA4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CE8863X94rR3vBgFBLmznN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-3urlck35/work/answers.sh","content":"#!/bin/bash\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../skill\" || exit 1\nP=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python\nA=\"$P scripts/answer.py ../agent/brace-findings.json\"\n\n# B01\n$A check B01.1 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:20 --quote 'const ALLOWED = new Set(allowlist.tools.map((t) => t.tool));' \\\n  --counter 'Searched for *, mcp__*, Bash(*), bypassPermissions, regex entries and list_tools-derived lists in config/ and src/. Only config/tools.allowlist.yaml lists tools, all literal names. reminders.ts has no model or tools.' \\\n  --note 'One fixed allowlist of literal tool names is loaded for the scheduling_agent role.'\n$A check B01.2 --met no --evidence src/agent/loop.ts:50 --quote 'const tools = registry.definitions();' \\\n  --note 'definitions() returns every tool the metadata scanner accepted (registry.ts:84-86). Nothing filters by the allowlist before the model sees them, so any extra EHR MCP tool (for example get_patient_contact or list_appointments_by_date) is offered to the model. The allowlist only bites later, at call time.'\n$A check B01.3 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:55 --quote 'if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\"not_allowlisted\");' \\\n  --counter 'Searched for getattr, globals, eval, registry[ , direct callTool fallbacks and catch blocks that continue on unknown tools. tool.invoke has one call site (executor.ts:86), after the allowlist and registry checks; ehr.call is invoked by native code with fixed tool names only.' \\\n  --note 'Unlisted names are denied and audited before lookup.'\n$A check B01.4 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:67 --quote 'if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {' \\\n  --counter 'Searched src/ and config/ for readOnlyHint, destructiveHint, annotations, description and auto-approve code. annotations are only scanned for hostile text (metadata-scan.ts:126). description is copied to the model definition (registry.ts:164) and never read by a permission branch.' \\\n  --note 'Allow and approval branches use only the tool name and static policy lists.'\n$A check B01.5 --met yes --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:102 --quote '- { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }' \\\n  --counter 'Searched for open(, fs., readFileSync, volumes and mountPath. No allowlisted tool reads files; harness reads use fixed paths (config.ts:41, identity.ts:27, identity.ts:112). Only /tmp (memory emptyDir) and a read-only token dir are mounted; no hostPath, no home or root mount.' \\\n  --note 'No file tool exists and mounts are limited to named directories.'\n\n# B02\n$A check B02.1 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' \\\n  --note 'The agent role gets PutItem and UpdateItem on every table matching clinic-agent-*. That covers the approvals and control (kill switch) tables, not only the budget table the agent writes. The secrets grant at iam.tf:35 is also a prefix wildcard (clinic-agent/*) across all clinics. No bare * and no admin role.'\n$A check B02.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' \\\n  --note 'The tenant for every tool call comes from a clinicId the model fills in, for every caller including SMS patients. It selects the per-clinic EHR, payments and SMS credentials (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12). Nothing checks it against ctx.tenantId or the caller. The runtime role can read every clinic secret (iam.tf:35).'\n$A check B02.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 --quote 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' \\\n  --note 'The EHR token request sends scope but no audience or resource. Payments and SMS use static keys with no audience. Only the eligibility exchange (eligibility-a2a.ts:43) sets an audience.'\n$A check B02.4 --met unknown --note 'Looked in ehr-mcp.ts, payments.ts, sms.ts, eligibility-a2a.ts and iam.tf. The AWS role is agent-only (iam.tf:1-2) and the eligibility exchange uses the agent workload token (eligibility-a2a.ts:41). No personal session is copied. Whether the EHR, payments and SMS providers identify the agent separately depends on provider-side client and key setup outside this repo.'\n\n# B03\n$A check B03.1 --met unknown --note 'EHR gets 5-minute access tokens via client_credentials (ehr-mcp.ts:12). Payments and SMS read a static restricted_key / api_token from Secrets Manager at run time (payments.ts:13, sms.ts:25). Whether those providers offer federated or short-lived credentials is not stated in the repo.'\n$A check B03.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/main.tf:82 --quote 'resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {' \\\n  --note 'No rotation resource, rotation lambda, TTL or lifetime is set for the EHR client secrets, payments keys or SMS tokens (main.tf:77-90). Searched the repo for rotat, lifetime, ttl and expir; only EHR access-token expiry (ehr-mcp.ts:45) and the IRSA token (deployment.yaml:18) are bounded.'\n$A check B03.3 --met yes --evidence Dockerfile:12 --quote 'ENV NODE_ENV=production' \\\n  --counter 'Grepped the whole repo for sk-, AKIA, password, secret:, token:, api_key. Hits were only code identifiers, ARNs and Secrets Manager names, no values. No .env files, .tfvars or .mcp.json exist. The system prompt only substitutes clinicName.' \\\n  --note 'Secrets live only in Secrets Manager.'\n$A check B03.4 --met unknown --note 'EHR, payments, SMS and eligibility calls all use plain bearer tokens (ehr-mcp.ts:58, payments.ts:33, eligibility-a2a.ts:61). The EHR connection only pins the server certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:20), with no client cert or DPoP. Whether the providers support holder binding is not stated in the repo.'\n\n# B04\n$A check B04.1 --met unknown --note 'The runtime role is agent-only (iam.tf:1-2), so disabling it would not touch users. The repo has no runbook or script to disable that role or rotate the EHR, payments or SMS credentials. The ops role can only write the control table (iam.tf:82). Credential revocation may live in AWS or the providers.'\n$A check B04.2 --met no --evidence src/control/kill-switch.ts:48 --quote 'async assertRunning(tenantId: string): Promise<void> {' \\\n  --note 'The only stop control is a flag in a DynamoDB table that the agent reads and obeys (kill-switch.ts:5-7, executor.ts:59). It runs inside the agent process. Credentials are not revoked at any gateway, IdP or target service, so a compromised or non-cooperating process keeps working.'\n$A check B04.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/payments.ts:33 --quote 'authorization: `Bearer ${await key(clinicId)}`,' \\\n  --note 'No revocation time limit is stated anywhere. Payments and SMS use static keys with no expiry. EHR tokens are cached up to 5 minutes (ehr-mcp.ts:34) and sessions up to 4 minutes (ehr-mcp.ts:69). Nothing introspects tokens or pushes revocation (CAEP).'\n$A check B04.4 --met no --evidence README.md:41 --quote 'aws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\' \\\n  --note 'The documented cutoff only sets the halted flag. It revokes no refresh token, access token, session or stored credential. Cached EHR tokens and sessions stay valid (ehr-mcp.ts:34, 52-53).'\n\n# B05\n$A check B05.1 --met no --evidence config/tools.allowlist.yaml:17 --quote 'reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.' \\\n  --note 'highImpactTools lists only cancel_appointment, refund_deposit and send_freeform (policy.yaml:5-8). ehr__update_appointment can set status to cancelled, a destructive update, and is not listed. Unlisted allowlisted tools run with no approval. No audit-deletion tool exists.'\n$A check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/approvals.ts:81 --quote 'return { ok: true, approval: rec };' \\\n  --note 'checkApproval receives args (approvals.ts:64) but never compares them to the stored argsHash (approvals.ts:49). An approval for one deposit refund or SMS body authorizes any other arguments for the same tool and clinic. The approver summary also omits clinicId (executor.ts:64). The gate does run before the side effect and is not in a try/catch.'\n$A check B05.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --quote 'const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(' \\\n  --note 'insurance__check_eligibility refunds a deposit itself, with no approval, when a peer reply says depositWaived. That is the same operation payments__refund_deposit gates. Also ehr__update_appointment with status cancelled does what the gated cancel tool does (allowlist line 17). The gate keys on tool name only.'\n$A check B05.4 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:41 --quote '\"dynamodb:PutItem\",' \\\n  --note 'The approver is the staff console (main.tf:11-12), but the agent runtime role can PutItem and UpdateItem on the approvals table through clinic-agent-* (iam.tf:41-47). checkApproval trusts any record with status approved and an approverRole string (approvals.ts:74-80), with no proof it was written by the console. The agent identity can therefore forge its own approval. Model prompts are not the enforcement and timeouts do not proceed.'\n$A check B05.5 --met no --evidence config/tools.allowlist.yaml:16 --quote '- tool: ehr__update_appointment' \\\n  --note 'The agent reads untrusted patient text and tool results, reaches PHI, and acts outside (SMS, refunds, appointment changes). ehr__update_appointment, ehr__book_appointment and sms__send_to_patient run ungated with model-chosen arguments, and the eligibility refund also runs ungated. There is no plan-then-execute or capability tracking in the code.'\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":713,"cache_read_input_tokens":97818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":713},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a681a98f-3aae-4114-80b6-e645e51f39d2","uuid":"a43188d8-ebed-4f73-883f-d59e928bc122","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:18:35.888Z","request_id":"req_011CgDUXr39CZgjhX7CJqCkn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CE8863X94rR3vBgFBLmznN":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-3urlck35/work/answers.sh","content":"#!/bin/bash\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../skill\" || exit 1\nP=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python\nA=\"$P scripts/answer.py ../agent/brace-findings.json\"\n\n# B01\n$A check B01.1 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:20 --quote 'const ALLOWED = new Set(allowlist.tools.map((t) => t.tool));' \\\n  --counter 'Searched for *, mcp__*, Bash(*), bypassPermissions, regex entries and list_tools-derived lists in config/ and src/. Only config/tools.allowlist.yaml lists tools, all literal names. reminders.ts has no model or tools.' \\\n  --note 'One fixed allowlist of literal tool names is loaded for the scheduling_agent role.'\n$A check B01.2 --met no --evidence src/agent/loop.ts:50 --quote 'const tools = registry.definitions();' \\\n  --note 'definitions() returns every tool the metadata scanner accepted (registry.ts:84-86). Nothing filters by the allowlist before the model sees them, so any extra EHR MCP tool (for example get_patient_contact or list_appointments_by_date) is offered to the model. The allowlist only bites later, at call time.'\n$A check B01.3 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:55 --quote 'if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\"not_allowlisted\");' \\\n  --counter 'Searched for getattr, globals, eval, registry[ , direct callTool fallbacks and catch blocks that continue on unknown tools. tool.invoke has one call site (executor.ts:86), after the allowlist and registry checks; ehr.call is invoked by native code with fixed tool names only.' \\\n  --note 'Unlisted names are denied and audited before lookup.'\n$A check B01.4 --met yes --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:67 --quote 'if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {' \\\n  --counter 'Searched src/ and config/ for readOnlyHint, destructiveHint, annotations, description and auto-approve code. annotations are only scanned for hostile text (metadata-scan.ts:126). description is copied to the model definition (registry.ts:164) and never read by a permission branch.' \\\n  --note 'Allow and approval branches use only the tool name and static policy lists.'\n$A check B01.5 --met yes --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:102 --quote '- { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }' \\\n  --counter 'Searched for open(, fs., readFileSync, volumes and mountPath. No allowlisted tool reads files; harness reads use fixed paths (config.ts:41, identity.ts:27, identity.ts:112). Only /tmp (memory emptyDir) and a read-only token dir are mounted; no hostPath, no home or root mount.' \\\n  --note 'No file tool exists and mounts are limited to named directories.'\n\n# B02\n$A check B02.1 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' \\\n  --note 'The agent role gets PutItem and UpdateItem on every table matching clinic-agent-*. That covers the approvals and control (kill switch) tables, not only the budget table the agent writes. The secrets grant at iam.tf:35 is also a prefix wildcard (clinic-agent/*) across all clinics. No bare * and no admin role.'\n$A check B02.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' \\\n  --note 'The tenant for every tool call comes from a clinicId the model fills in, for every caller including SMS patients. It selects the per-clinic EHR, payments and SMS credentials (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12). Nothing checks it against ctx.tenantId or the caller. The runtime role can read every clinic secret (iam.tf:35).'\n$A check B02.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 --quote 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' \\\n  --note 'The EHR token request sends scope but no audience or resource. Payments and SMS use static keys with no audience. Only the eligibility exchange (eligibility-a2a.ts:43) sets an audience.'\n$A check B02.4 --met unknown --note 'Looked in ehr-mcp.ts, payments.ts, sms.ts, eligibility-a2a.ts and iam.tf. The AWS role is agent-only (iam.tf:1-2) and the eligibility exchange uses the agent workload token (eligibility-a2a.ts:41). No personal session is copied. Whether the EHR, payments and SMS providers identify the agent separately depends on provider-side client and key setup outside this repo.'\n\n# B03\n$A check B03.1 --met unknown --note 'EHR gets 5-minute access tokens via client_credentials (ehr-mcp.ts:12). Payments and SMS read a static restricted_key / api_token from Secrets Manager at run time (payments.ts:13, sms.ts:25). Whether those providers offer federated or short-lived credentials is not stated in the repo.'\n$A check B03.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/main.tf:82 --quote 'resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {' \\\n  --note 'No rotation resource, rotation lambda, TTL or lifetime is set for the EHR client secrets, payments keys or SMS tokens (main.tf:77-90). Searched the repo for rotat, lifetime, ttl and expir; only EHR access-token expiry (ehr-mcp.ts:45) and the IRSA token (deployment.yaml:18) are bounded.'\n$A check B03.3 --met yes --evidence Dockerfile:12 --quote 'ENV NODE_ENV=production' \\\n  --counter 'Grepped the whole repo for sk-, AKIA, password, secret:, token:, api_key. Hits were only code identifiers, ARNs and Secrets Manager names, no values. No .env files, .tfvars or .mcp.json exist. The system prompt only substitutes clinicName.' \\\n  --note 'Secrets live only in Secrets Manager.'\n$A check B03.4 --met unknown --note 'EHR, payments, SMS and eligibility calls all use plain bearer tokens (ehr-mcp.ts:58, payments.ts:33, eligibility-a2a.ts:61). The EHR connection only pins the server certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:20), with no client cert or DPoP. Whether the providers support holder binding is not stated in the repo.'\n\n# B04\n$A check B04.1 --met unknown --note 'The runtime role is agent-only (iam.tf:1-2), so disabling it would not touch users. The repo has no runbook or script to disable that role or rotate the EHR, payments or SMS credentials. The ops role can only write the control table (iam.tf:82). Credential revocation may live in AWS or the providers.'\n$A check B04.2 --met no --evidence src/control/kill-switch.ts:48 --quote 'async assertRunning(tenantId: string): Promise<void> {' \\\n  --note 'The only stop control is a flag in a DynamoDB table that the agent reads and obeys (kill-switch.ts:5-7, executor.ts:59). It runs inside the agent process. Credentials are not revoked at any gateway, IdP or target service, so a compromised or non-cooperating process keeps working.'\n$A check B04.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/payments.ts:33 --quote 'authorization: `Bearer ${await key(clinicId)}`,' \\\n  --note 'No revocation time limit is stated anywhere. Payments and SMS use static keys with no expiry. EHR tokens are cached up to 5 minutes (ehr-mcp.ts:34) and sessions up to 4 minutes (ehr-mcp.ts:69). Nothing introspects tokens or pushes revocation (CAEP).'\n$A check B04.4 --met no --evidence README.md:41 --quote 'aws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\' \\\n  --note 'The documented cutoff only sets the halted flag. It revokes no refresh token, access token, session or stored credential. Cached EHR tokens and sessions stay valid (ehr-mcp.ts:34, 52-53).'\n\n# B05\n$A check B05.1 --met no --evidence config/tools.allowlist.yaml:17 --quote 'reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.' \\\n  --note 'highImpactTools lists only cancel_appointment, refund_deposit and send_freeform (policy.yaml:5-8). ehr__update_appointment can set status to cancelled, a destructive update, and is not listed. Unlisted allowlisted tools run with no approval. No audit-deletion tool exists.'\n$A check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/approvals.ts:81 --quote 'return { ok: true, approval: rec };' \\\n  --note 'checkApproval receives args (approvals.ts:64) but never compares them to the stored argsHash (approvals.ts:49). An approval for one deposit refund or SMS body authorizes any other arguments for the same tool and clinic. The approver summary also omits clinicId (executor.ts:64). The gate does run before the side effect and is not in a try/catch.'\n$A check B05.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --quote 'const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(' \\\n  --note 'insurance__check_eligibility refunds a deposit itself, with no approval, when a peer reply says depositWaived. That is the same operation payments__refund_deposit gates. Also ehr__update_appointment with status cancelled does what the gated cancel tool does (allowlist line 17). The gate keys on tool name only.'\n$A check B05.4 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:41 --quote '\"dynamodb:PutItem\",' \\\n  --note 'The approver is the staff console (main.tf:11-12), but the agent runtime role can PutItem and UpdateItem on the approvals table through clinic-agent-* (iam.tf:41-47). checkApproval trusts any record with status approved and an approverRole string (approvals.ts:74-80), with no proof it was written by the console. The agent identity can therefore forge its own approval. Model prompts are not the enforcement and timeouts do not proceed.'\n$A check B05.5 --met no --evidence config/tools.allowlist.yaml:16 --quote '- tool: ehr__update_appointment' \\\n  --note 'The agent reads untrusted patient text and tool results, reaches PHI, and acts outside (SMS, refunds, appointment changes). ehr__update_appointment, ehr__book_appointment and sms__send_to_patient run ungated with model-chosen arguments, and the eligibility refund also runs ungated. There is no plan-then-execute or capability tracking in the code.'\n"}}}
