{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDUgjL4gCrbVCfZG7c3y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and all five are rated `gap`. The batch validator printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.` with `--batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges`. The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I didn't run challenges, and no other items were touched.\n\n**Findings by item**\n\n- **B01 (minimal tool surface):**\n  - The allowlist is a fixed literal list and the dispatcher denies anything not on it (`executor.ts:55`).\n  - The model is still shown every EHR tool the scanner accepts (`loop.ts:50`, `registry.ts:84-86`), not only the allowlisted ones.\n  - B01.1, B01.3, B01.4 and B01.5 are `yes`.\n- **B02 (least privilege):**\n  - The model chooses `clinicId` for every call, including from SMS patients. That value selects the clinic's EHR, payments and SMS credentials (`executor.ts:63`).\n  - The runtime IAM role has prefix wildcards over all `clinic-agent-*` tables and `clinic-agent/*` secrets (`iam.tf:35,47`).\n  - The EHR token request has no audience (`ehr-mcp.ts:41`).\n  - B02.4 is `unknown`, because provider-side identity isn't in the repo.\n- **B03 (credential lifetime):**\n  - No rotation or lifetime is configured for the EHR, payments or SMS secrets (`main.tf:161-175`).\n  - B03.3 is `yes`: I found no secret values checked in.\n  - B03.1 and B03.4 are `unknown`, because provider support for short-lived or holder-bound credentials isn't stated.\n- **B04 (independent revocation):**\n  - The only cutoff is a halt flag that the agent reads itself (`kill-switch.ts:48`).\n  - No revocation time limit is stated. Payments and SMS use static keys, and cached EHR tokens and sessions stay valid.\n  - B04.1 is `unknown`, because the repo has no runbook for disabling the agent role or rotating provider credentials.\n- **B05 (destructive-action interception):**\n  - `ehr__update_appointment` can set status to cancelled but isn't in `highImpactTools`.\n  - `checkApproval` never compares the stored `argsHash` to the arguments (`approvals.ts:81`).\n  - `insurance__check_eligibility` refunds a deposit with no approval (`eligibility-check.ts:40`).\n  - The agent role can write to the approvals table (`iam.tf:41-47`), so it could forge an approval. I rated B05.4 `no` on that IAM evidence at medium confidence.\n\n**Prescan hits:** I dismissed H005 (B02). It is `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken` on the CI deploy role, which AWS only allows on `Resource *`, and it isn't attached to the agent's identity. The other hits (H001–H004 B11, H006–H010 R13, H011 E03) belong to items outside this batch, so I left them unresolved.\n\n**Other notes**\n\n- Outside this batch, the SMS webhook logs a failed signature check and then keeps processing the request (`sms-webhook.ts:50-54`). That's worth a look in a later batch.\n- I filled in `scope`, which was still the starter placeholder. I did that with a small script, since `answer.py` has no scope option.\n- My working scripts are in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":113069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":637},"output_tokens":825,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a681a98f-3aae-4114-80b6-e645e51f39d2","uuid":"b00eb61a-372e-4e5e-b486-78c4e7406be6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:20:14.109Z","request_id":"req_011CgDUgj2iF4QGXbtfhVwaY"}
